-- Six units on a battlefield: Damage, Speed, Range, Cooldown are stats; threat and dps are defs computed from them, columns that exist only while a statement looks at them. A def can be written into a real column, tested, folded, and sorted by.
-- threat evaluates to 20 30 120 200 40 20 against pre-state; the masked write gathers the derived cells for the selected rows first.
-- Rows 0 and 5 keep priority 9 (not Enemy); row 5 keeps Dangerous without Enemy; rows 2 and 3 gain it.
--! registry ../registries/020-derived-columns.reg
--! expect priority = 9 30 120 200 40 9
--! expect dangerous = 0 0 1 1 0 1

def threat = Damage * Speed / Range
def dps    = Damage / Cooldown
Enemy , Priority = threat
Enemy & threat > 100 , +Dangerous
--! out 390
+/ threat @ Enemy
--! out 25
+/ dps @ Enemy
-- descending grade is stable: the tie 20 at rows 0 and 5 grades in source order, 0 before 5
--! out 3 2 4 1 0 5
order by threat desc
